# This repository is LF on disk, and that is load-bearing.
#
# `lib/client.core.js`, `lib/client.scene.js` and `lib/client.menu.js` are delivered COPIES of
# `lib/core.js`, `lib/scene.js` and `lib/menu.js`, and `scripts/client-chunks.mjs --check` decides whether
# they are stale by comparing them BYTE FOR BYTE against a fresh generation — which emits LF. On a Windows
# checkout with Git's `core.autocrlf=true` (Git for Windows' default) every file comes back CRLF, so that
# check is guaranteed to fail with three "stale chunk" reports that are not stale at all. Measured on a
# fresh clone of this repository, 2026-10-11: identical hashes to the ones a Windows developer sees, and the
# tree was clean. `scripts/vendor-build.mjs --check` compares the committed 3D chunk the same way.
#
# Pinning the checkout to LF is what keeps those two checks meaningful instead of noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, named explicitly so that auto-detection is never the only thing standing between a model
# file and a line-ending rewrite.
*.vrm binary
*.vrma binary
*.br binary
*.png binary
*.apng binary
